WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.500
Let's follow the path of Dusty's trail, oh Dusty's trail, Dusty's trail

00:07.500 --> 00:16.000
A stage and a wagon ahead and west, part of a wagon train lost from the rest

00:16.000 --> 00:23.500
Dusty's the reason for their flight, thanks to Dusty nothing's right

00:23.500 --> 00:31.000
Only the wagon master's hand keeps them a-rollin' through the promised land

00:31.000 --> 00:37.000
All that goin' gets mighty rough, but they don't seem to mind

00:37.000 --> 00:43.000
It's California, eh, that's the place they must find

00:43.000 --> 00:50.000
Deserts and rocks are in their way, but they won't stop, come what may

00:50.000 --> 00:55.000
Mountains and hills that they must scale, but they know they'll make it

00:55.000 --> 01:00.000
Cause they just can't fail on Dusty's trail

01:03.000 --> 01:06.000
I don't know, it's supposed to be Buffalo Country, I haven't seen one

01:06.000 --> 01:07.000
I saw one

01:07.000 --> 01:08.000
Why didn't you shoot him?

01:08.000 --> 01:11.000
I didn't want to make him mad, did you ever see the horns on one of those fellas?

01:11.000 --> 01:13.000
Yeah, yeah

01:13.000 --> 01:18.000
Well, I guess we ought to get on back, rest of them ought to be awake by now, huh?

01:18.000 --> 01:20.000
I kind of hate to leave this place, it's so peaceful

01:20.000 --> 01:22.000
Yeah, sure is

01:25.000 --> 01:26.000
Here

01:28.000 --> 01:29.000
I think we got company

01:29.000 --> 01:33.000
What, are you crazy? Nobody around here, miles and miles, miles

01:33.000 --> 01:34.000
Oh, hi neighbor

01:34.000 --> 01:35.000
Nice day, isn't it?

01:35.000 --> 01:36.000
Sure, try em'

01:36.000 --> 01:40.000
Hey, be careful where you're pointing those guns, fellas, Mr. Callahan's kind of tough

01:40.000 --> 01:44.000
I don't like nobody pointing guns at me till I've been properly introduced

01:53.000 --> 01:56.000
Well, now here, I'm certainly glad to make your acquaintance, sir

01:56.000 --> 01:58.000
Yes, sir, yes, sir

01:58.000 --> 02:10.000
Oh, yes, sir, yes, sir

02:20.000 --> 02:26.000
Hey, listen, are you guys after money? I mean, I got some in the bank in Kansas City, I'd be happy to go get it for you

02:26.000 --> 02:28.000
I'll help him carry it

02:28.000 --> 02:31.000
Mister, one more step and your wife will be a widow

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
Oh, well, I'm not married, I wasn't really stepping on anybody

02:33.000 --> 02:35.000
Then your wife will be a widow

02:35.000 --> 02:37.000
I'm not even gazed, but I'm not stepping either, see

02:37.000 --> 02:42.000
Yes, sir, you're just the guys we're looking for

02:42.000 --> 02:44.000
Well, if you're not after money, what do you want?

02:44.000 --> 02:46.000
Might be something to cheer up our sisters

02:46.000 --> 02:48.000
Where have Ira and Cleo?

02:48.000 --> 02:53.000
Practically to the altar, when Clarence and Harvey haven't cashed in their chips

02:53.000 --> 02:57.000
Oh, that's too bad, what did they die of?

02:57.000 --> 03:00.000
You might say it's a bad case of lead poisoning

03:00.000 --> 03:04.000
Accident? Noof, more like on purpose

03:04.000 --> 03:10.000
Oh, well, I can see how your sisters will ease them, cheering up, sure enough, losing their grooms like that

03:10.000 --> 03:13.000
Yeah, we'll be happy to cheer him up, but Mr. Callahan can tell him jokes

03:13.000 --> 03:17.000
Right, he does great turkey gobbler, he does it so good we almost lost him on Thanksgiving

03:17.000 --> 03:23.000
That's not exactly what we had in mind, we were thinking about words you might say

03:23.000 --> 03:26.000
Words would make them gals happy again

03:26.000 --> 03:28.000
What words? Just two short ones

03:28.000 --> 03:30.000
I do, you don't

03:30.000 --> 03:32.000
We do

03:32.000 --> 03:35.000
Listen, we don't even know your sisters, they gotta be kidding

03:35.000 --> 03:37.000
They're not kidding

03:44.000 --> 03:45.000
Is anything wrong?

03:45.000 --> 03:47.000
Callahan and Dusty aren't here

03:47.000 --> 03:50.000
Oh, well last night they said they were going hunting this morning

03:50.000 --> 03:53.000
And the horses are all here, they must have gone on foot

03:53.000 --> 03:56.000
Well now in that case we ought to be able to track them

03:56.000 --> 04:00.000
Here's some footprints leading away from the wagon

04:00.000 --> 04:04.000
What do you say we follow them Mr. Brookhaven?

04:04.000 --> 04:08.000
I'm a banker, not a bloodhound

04:08.000 --> 04:10.000
Come on, tell me

04:10.000 --> 04:15.000
Oh, very well

04:15.000 --> 04:18.000
We'll just wait right here while Buck gets the girls

04:18.000 --> 04:21.000
You're about to meet up with two pretty fillies

04:21.000 --> 04:22.000
Pretty what?

04:22.000 --> 04:25.000
Careful mister, you're talking about my sisters

04:25.000 --> 04:28.000
I was only joking, I mean you asked us to be cheerful

04:28.000 --> 04:30.000
Yeah, that's what we are, cheerful

04:30.000 --> 04:32.000
Then how about a smile?

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
Yeah, we're smiling, but from the inside

04:35.000 --> 04:37.000
Yeah, just on the outside we're miserable

04:37.000 --> 04:40.000
I'll give you something to be happy about

04:40.000 --> 04:42.000
In about two minutes you're going to be popping the question

04:42.000 --> 04:45.000
And Elvira and Cleo will be saying yes

04:45.000 --> 04:49.000
Yeah, well maybe they won't say yes, maybe they won't even like us

04:49.000 --> 04:51.000
Oh, they'll like you alright

04:51.000 --> 04:53.000
Well, what if we don't like them?

04:53.000 --> 04:55.000
You'll like them

04:55.000 --> 04:57.000
We'll like them

05:04.000 --> 05:06.000
I think I kind of envy those guys out there under the dirt

05:06.000 --> 05:08.000
I think they took the easy way out

05:08.000 --> 05:10.000
Elvira, meet up with them

05:10.000 --> 05:11.000
Yeah, yeah, count of hands

05:11.000 --> 05:13.000
My name is, this is Dusty

05:13.000 --> 05:14.000
Howdy

05:14.000 --> 05:15.000
Howdy

05:15.000 --> 05:16.000
Howdy

05:16.000 --> 05:17.000
Howdy

05:17.000 --> 05:20.000
Come on Cleo, before it's coming six is a crowd

05:20.000 --> 05:23.000
The boys here have something to ask you

05:23.000 --> 05:25.000
We'll be right outside

05:25.000 --> 05:27.000
I kind of like the big one

05:27.000 --> 05:31.000
Oh alright, then I'll take the shrimp

05:31.000 --> 05:33.000
Come on boys, let's sit down

05:33.000 --> 05:36.000
Oh yes, yes

05:36.000 --> 05:38.000
Buck says yes to everything you want to ask him

05:38.000 --> 05:40.000
Ask him? No, I can't think of anything

05:40.000 --> 05:42.000
Can you think of anything that we were going to ask him?

05:42.000 --> 05:44.000
I can't think of anything I'd ask him

05:44.000 --> 05:48.000
I'm sure Clint said you had a question you all wanted to ask us

05:48.000 --> 05:50.000
Oh that question, yes

05:50.000 --> 05:52.000
The boys told us that we had to ask you

05:52.000 --> 05:56.000
I mean they told us that we wanted to ask you if

05:56.000 --> 05:58.000
We couldn't all have a drink

05:58.000 --> 06:00.000
That's the question, right

06:00.000 --> 06:03.000
I was going to say that sounds like a good idea

06:03.000 --> 06:06.000
Yeah, help us all get better acquainted

06:06.000 --> 06:08.000
We'll be right back

06:12.000 --> 06:15.000
Let's get out of here while we're still alive and single

06:15.000 --> 06:17.000
Come on

06:18.000 --> 06:20.000
We're alive, free and single

06:20.000 --> 06:22.000
Hey, stop talking, let's start running

06:25.000 --> 06:27.000
Going somewhere?

06:27.000 --> 06:30.000
Well, we were just going out for a little air, you see

06:30.000 --> 06:32.000
It was warm in there

06:32.000 --> 06:36.000
Warm was it? I can put a few holes in you to cool you off

06:43.000 --> 06:46.000
You don't have to tie us up, we're not going anywhere

06:46.000 --> 06:47.000
You're booching or not

06:47.000 --> 06:49.000
You fellas might as well know the truth

06:49.000 --> 06:51.000
Buck and me, we're desperate

06:51.000 --> 06:54.000
We want to get to California, make a support

06:54.000 --> 06:57.000
But we promised Plump on his deathbed that we wouldn't leave the gals

06:57.000 --> 07:00.000
Unless they was hitched and had somebody to take care of

07:00.000 --> 07:02.000
Well, why us, why not somebody else?

07:02.000 --> 07:05.000
Because you're here and somebody else ain't

07:05.000 --> 07:07.000
We got a plate in their faehood side anymore

07:07.000 --> 07:10.000
We had two other guys all set, but they tried to run out of us

07:10.000 --> 07:13.000
So you see, you ain't got much choice

07:13.000 --> 07:17.000
It's either marrying or joining Clarence and Harvey out there

07:17.000 --> 07:21.000
Oh, yeah, the more I think about it, the more attractive those ladies get

07:21.000 --> 07:23.000
Good thinking, mister

07:23.000 --> 07:25.000
Yeah, yeah

07:31.000 --> 07:32.000
Why did you say that?

07:32.000 --> 07:34.000
I'm not marrying either one of those girls and my life depends on it

07:34.000 --> 07:35.000
Neither am I

07:35.000 --> 07:38.000
I'm just trying to give ourselves a breathing spell till we can break out of here

07:38.000 --> 07:40.000
You had me worried for a minute

07:40.000 --> 07:43.000
Hey, listen, see if you can reach the notch down on my wrist, will you?

07:43.000 --> 07:44.000
Okay

07:44.000 --> 07:46.000
Oh, I think I've got it

07:46.000 --> 07:47.000
Yeah? Yeah

07:47.000 --> 07:48.000
Good

07:48.000 --> 07:49.000
I've got it, yeah, yeah

07:49.000 --> 07:50.000
Okay

07:49.000 --> 07:50.000
I'm working on it, yeah

07:50.000 --> 07:52.000
I'm getting it, I'm getting it

07:52.000 --> 07:53.000
Nope

07:53.000 --> 07:54.000
No, no? What happened?

07:54.000 --> 07:56.000
I've been tugging on my thumb

07:57.000 --> 07:59.000
Oh, good, good, good

07:59.000 --> 08:02.000
Listen, there's just one little latch on that door

08:02.000 --> 08:05.000
Maybe if we can kind of jump over there, you know?

08:05.000 --> 08:06.000
Oh, okay

08:06.000 --> 08:07.000
All right, let's get a try

08:07.000 --> 08:08.000
Here you go

08:08.000 --> 08:09.000
Oh, there

08:12.000 --> 08:15.000
Oh, now wait, whoa, whoa, we're not getting nowhere this time

08:15.000 --> 08:17.000
Have you ever been to Papoose?

08:17.000 --> 08:18.000
Papoose?

08:18.000 --> 08:21.000
Yeah, you know how to carry them Indian kids on the back?

08:21.000 --> 08:23.000
Hang tight

08:30.000 --> 08:32.000
Oh, yeah, yeah, get to the door

08:32.000 --> 08:33.000
Okay

08:33.000 --> 08:35.000
No more, no more, no more of this way

08:35.000 --> 08:36.000
That's it, come on

08:36.000 --> 08:37.000
I got it, there it is

08:37.000 --> 08:39.000
Whoa, listen, we're free, we're free

08:39.000 --> 08:41.000
I don't know how I'm going to thank you, Mr. Callahan, for saving my life

08:41.000 --> 08:42.000
Will you stop blubbering?

08:42.000 --> 08:44.000
Let's just get out of here

08:44.000 --> 08:47.000
What's the matter?

08:47.000 --> 08:49.000
That's the matter

08:51.000 --> 08:53.000
Do you see what I see?

08:53.000 --> 08:56.000
I do, but I don't believe it

08:56.000 --> 08:58.000
Getting some more fresh air?

08:58.000 --> 09:00.000
No, we were trying to escape

09:00.000 --> 09:01.000
Dr.

09:01.000 --> 09:04.860
Don't know why you fellas are carrying the

09:04.860 --> 09:06.000
stuff that you're carrying

09:06.000 --> 09:08.000
I'm not carrying anything

09:08.000 --> 09:09.000
You're carrying what?

09:09.000 --> 09:11.000
The stuff that you're carrying

09:11.000 --> 09:14.000
I'm trying to escape

09:14.000 --> 09:16.000
Don't know why you fellas are carrying on so

09:16.000 --> 09:18.000
We ain't asking you to love them gals

09:18.000 --> 09:20.000
All you gotta do is marry them

09:20.000 --> 09:22.000
Yeah, but we'd make lousy husbands

09:22.000 --> 09:24.000
We like to be bachelors

09:24.000 --> 09:26.000
Every man likes being the best

09:26.000 --> 09:28.000
We all gotta go sometime

09:28.000 --> 09:31.000
This time everything's going to be done proper like

09:31.000 --> 09:36.000
First the courting, then hugging, then proposing

09:36.000 --> 09:39.000
First the courting, then hugging, then proposing

09:39.000 --> 09:41.000
In any order, you name it

09:41.000 --> 09:43.000
Maybe we ought to jump them

09:43.000 --> 09:44.000
Are you joking?

09:44.000 --> 09:46.000
Either one of those monstrous brutes could

09:46.000 --> 09:47.000
tear us in half

09:47.000 --> 09:49.000
Well we can't stand by and do nothing

09:49.000 --> 09:50.000
I have no intention to

09:50.000 --> 09:53.000
I was about to propose a very definite plan of action

09:53.000 --> 09:54.000
What?

09:54.000 --> 09:57.000
Let's go back to the wagon and tell the ladies we're in trouble

09:57.000 --> 10:00.000
Yeah, well I told once you ladies to think we're too forward

10:00.000 --> 10:02.000
But when you see beauty that's so overpowered

10:02.000 --> 10:04.000
It just makes your heart hammer

10:04.000 --> 10:06.000
Well there's just nothing you can do but come out and say so

10:06.000 --> 10:08.000
Now that's a mighty fine speech

10:08.000 --> 10:09.000
I agree

10:09.000 --> 10:10.000
You do?

10:10.000 --> 10:12.000
Yep, that was a mighty fine speech

10:12.000 --> 10:14.000
I was about to say the same thing myself

10:14.000 --> 10:16.000
You two girls are something else

10:16.000 --> 10:18.000
A few minutes ago you said you were going to be a

10:18.000 --> 10:19.000
You know what?

10:19.000 --> 10:20.000
I'm going to be a woman

10:20.000 --> 10:21.000
You're going to be a woman

10:21.000 --> 10:22.000
You're going to be a woman

10:22.000 --> 10:23.000
You're going to be a woman

10:23.000 --> 10:24.000
You're going to be a woman

10:24.000 --> 10:25.000
You're going to be a woman

10:25.000 --> 10:27.000
You're going to be a woman

10:27.000 --> 10:28.000
What else?

10:28.000 --> 10:32.000
A few minutes ago you acted like you could hardly wait to get out of here

10:32.000 --> 10:34.000
Yeah, we were just overcome by emotion

10:34.000 --> 10:37.000
You know, we just couldn't go on and speak out

10:37.000 --> 10:40.000
Yeah, we never met two girls like you before

10:40.000 --> 10:42.000
Dusty, don't pay these girls compliments like that

10:42.000 --> 10:45.000
They just must be hearing them all the time

10:45.000 --> 10:48.000
Papa used to say our eyes was prettier than the heifer's

10:48.000 --> 10:50.000
But don't you think I'm a little too

10:50.000 --> 10:52.000
Plump? Why fiddle sticks?

10:52.000 --> 10:54.000
I mean a girl would figure like yours

10:54.000 --> 10:56.000
Pardon me. Oh.

10:56.000 --> 10:59.000
You boys certainly know how to sweet talk a girl.

10:59.000 --> 11:03.000
No, that ain't sweet talk. I mean, not when you got a proper inspiration.

11:03.000 --> 11:05.000
Yeah, and we got plenty of inspiration.

11:05.000 --> 11:08.000
Uh, listen, would you, uh, would you pardon us?

11:08.000 --> 11:10.000
This is Mr. Dusty. Come in.

11:14.000 --> 11:17.000
Oh, that's the moment of truth. Which one you want?

11:17.000 --> 11:20.000
It's like having a choice between being trampled by an elephant or eaten by a buzzard.

11:20.000 --> 11:22.000
Yeah. Well, I'll take the elephants.

11:22.000 --> 11:24.000
I'll take the bug.

11:26.000 --> 11:29.000
Well, now, Alvary, uh, I haven't known you for very long,

11:29.000 --> 11:32.000
but there's something that I've got to ask you.

11:32.000 --> 11:36.000
Big Boy, if you're proposing, the answer is yeah!

11:36.000 --> 11:37.000
Yeah, yeah, yeah, well.

11:37.000 --> 11:41.000
Leo, there comes a time in every man's life when he wishes he was dead.

11:41.000 --> 11:43.000
I mean, he wishes he was dead right when he chooses his girl.

11:43.000 --> 11:45.000
I guess I'm...

11:45.000 --> 11:52.000
Sweetheart, I accept.

11:58.000 --> 12:01.000
I've got it. I've got just the thing.

12:01.000 --> 12:02.000
Andy, what is it?

12:02.000 --> 12:07.000
Well, I remember reading in a new scientific journal about a chemical discovery.

12:07.000 --> 12:09.000
I think I've succeeded in duplicating the formula.

12:09.000 --> 12:13.000
Andy, this is no time to be playing mad scientist.

12:13.000 --> 12:15.000
Callahan and Dusty are in trouble.

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
If this chemical does just half of what it's supposed to do,

12:18.000 --> 12:22.000
Callahan and Dusty will soon be free as birds.

12:22.000 --> 12:24.000
Bachelor birds.

12:31.000 --> 12:33.000
Welcome to the family, brothers-in-law.

12:33.000 --> 12:37.000
Well, not just yet. I mean, you see, we believe in long engagements.

12:37.000 --> 12:39.000
Well, that's all right with us, right, Clint?

12:39.000 --> 12:41.000
Sure. Till tomorrow.

12:41.000 --> 12:46.000
Yep. The Marian preacher's coming by to hitch the gals up with Clearance and Harvey.

12:46.000 --> 12:49.000
There'll be a change in names, that's all.

12:49.000 --> 12:52.000
Sure nice to know the preacher won't be coming for naps.

13:00.000 --> 13:02.000
Those two men are still on guard.

13:02.000 --> 13:05.000
Are you sure this'll work?

13:05.000 --> 13:08.000
It's called chloroform.

13:08.000 --> 13:11.000
And according to that article I read, a couple of whiffs of this

13:11.000 --> 13:39.000
and those two bruisers will be hearing Rockabye Baby.

13:39.000 --> 13:43.000
Jumping horn-toed, but there.

13:43.000 --> 13:46.000
I must have died going to heaven.

13:46.000 --> 13:48.000
Howdy.

13:48.000 --> 13:50.000
Hi.

13:50.000 --> 13:53.000
We saw the house and we thought we'd say howdy.

13:53.000 --> 13:55.000
We hope you don't mind.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.000
Just, we don't mind. Can we glance?

13:57.000 --> 14:03.000
Heck no. Best thing that's happened around here since the sheriff fell off his horse and broke his leg.

14:03.000 --> 14:09.000
Well, we was thinking of opening up a dance school nearby and uh...

14:09.000 --> 14:11.000
A dance in school?

14:11.000 --> 14:16.000
Yeah. And I'll bet you I could teach you to do the waltz in just one little old lesson.

14:16.000 --> 14:20.000
Yeah, come here.

14:20.000 --> 14:25.000
Now why don't you take those big arms and put them around my little waist and watch my feet.

14:25.000 --> 14:30.000
Ready? One, two, three, one, two, three.

14:30.000 --> 14:32.000
You sure have a wonderful fatigue.

14:32.000 --> 14:34.000
Pretty good muscles too.

14:34.000 --> 14:35.000
What?

14:35.000 --> 14:37.000
Hey, you smell good.

14:37.000 --> 14:41.000
Oh, it's not me. It's my flowers. See?

14:41.000 --> 14:46.000
Well, this waltz is pure as fun.

14:46.000 --> 15:06.000
I, uh, I, uh...

15:06.000 --> 15:07.000
Betsy.

15:07.000 --> 15:09.000
Lulu. Hey, you're just in time.

15:09.000 --> 15:11.000
Yeah, the preacher's coming tomorrow to marry us.

15:11.000 --> 15:14.000
Not if we can help it.

15:14.000 --> 15:19.000
Oh, thank you. Thank you.

15:19.000 --> 15:21.000
Oh, boy, I tell you.

15:21.000 --> 15:23.000
Hey, how'd you get past the guards?

15:23.000 --> 15:25.000
Don't worry about them. They're in slumberland.

15:25.000 --> 15:28.000
Yeah, now listen, we'll go first to make sure the coast is clear.

15:28.000 --> 15:30.000
And when you hear an owl hoot, you come or run it.

15:30.000 --> 15:32.000
Run it. Right. Ow.

15:32.000 --> 15:33.000
Here we go. You got that.

15:33.000 --> 15:34.000
Uh-huh. Yeah.

15:34.000 --> 15:36.000
Oh, I'll never forget Lulu and Betsy for this.

15:36.000 --> 15:39.000
They saved us from a fate worse than...

15:39.000 --> 15:42.000
Hey, that sound like an owl to you.

15:42.000 --> 15:48.000
Oh.

15:48.000 --> 15:50.000
What are you starving for?

15:50.000 --> 15:52.000
I just thought of a way to show our appreciation to Betsy and Lulu.

15:52.000 --> 15:55.000
Oh?

15:55.000 --> 15:56.000
I'll give these to Betsy.

15:56.000 --> 15:59.000
Hey, that's a good idea. I'll give these to Lulu.

15:59.000 --> 16:00.000
Oh, I bet they'll really like these, huh?

16:00.000 --> 16:02.000
Hey, they smell good, don't they?

16:02.000 --> 16:03.000
Huh? Yeah.

16:03.000 --> 16:05.000
Better get going before it's too late.

16:05.000 --> 16:07.000
Hey, Dusty, there's no time to take it.

16:07.000 --> 16:30.000
No, no, no.

16:30.000 --> 16:34.000
And then Dusty and Callahan smelled the flowers and passed out.

16:34.000 --> 16:37.000
Now, you mustn't blame yourselves, my dears.

16:37.000 --> 16:39.000
Perhaps you can try again tomorrow.

16:39.000 --> 16:41.000
Tomorrow will be too late.

16:41.000 --> 16:43.000
The preacher comes tomorrow to tie the knots.

16:43.000 --> 16:44.000
That soon?

16:44.000 --> 16:50.000
Yeah. Just 24 little hours.

16:50.000 --> 17:05.000
Suppose the preacher were to arrive before tomorrow, like today, for example.

17:05.000 --> 17:24.000
All righty, brother.

17:24.000 --> 17:26.000
Don't let me stop your work.

17:26.000 --> 17:30.000
He who cuts his own wood is twice blessed.

17:30.000 --> 17:31.000
Amen.

17:31.000 --> 17:32.000
Amen.

17:32.000 --> 17:35.000
We weren't expecting preacher Waldo till tomorrow.

17:35.000 --> 17:38.000
I'm afraid the good brother was gone to his just desert.

17:38.000 --> 17:39.000
Gone?

17:39.000 --> 17:42.000
Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.

17:42.000 --> 17:43.000
Amen.

17:43.000 --> 17:44.000
Amen.

17:44.000 --> 17:47.000
Reverend Brookhaven is my name, brother.

17:47.000 --> 17:52.000
And this here is my helpmaid in joy and sorrow, Mrs. Reverend Brookhaven.

17:52.000 --> 17:54.000
Pleased to meet you.

17:54.000 --> 17:55.000
You a regular reverend.

17:55.000 --> 18:00.000
Or deemed by this book for preaching, funeralizing, and baptizing.

18:00.000 --> 18:02.000
How about weddings?

18:02.000 --> 18:05.000
When the reverend joins them, you can't separate them with a crowbar.

18:05.000 --> 18:11.000
Reverend, I think you and us can do some business.

18:11.000 --> 18:13.000
I just know I'm going to cry.

18:13.000 --> 18:16.000
I always cry at weddings.

18:16.000 --> 18:18.000
I know a couple men are going to cry at this wedding.

18:18.000 --> 18:22.000
Please, remind me. I'd better go get the grooms.

18:22.000 --> 18:25.000
Sure lucky thing for us reverend King.

18:25.000 --> 18:33.000
Well, here come the brides.

18:33.000 --> 18:35.000
It's a bead.

18:35.000 --> 18:39.000
This is cruel and a human punishment.

18:39.000 --> 18:40.000
Thank you, sir.

18:40.000 --> 18:41.000
It was beautiful.

18:41.000 --> 18:46.000
I've been practicing it for a long time.

18:46.000 --> 18:53.000
Swear, dang it.

18:53.000 --> 18:56.000
Brother and Rosal, I want you to meet the man who's going to do the honor.

18:56.000 --> 18:57.000
Reverend Brookhaven.

18:57.000 --> 18:58.000
Wait a minute, he's not a re...

18:58.000 --> 19:00.000
Don't be nervous friend.

19:00.000 --> 19:01.000
Just leave it to the reverend.

19:01.000 --> 19:07.000
As good book says, e pluribus unum, and caveat emtos.

19:07.000 --> 19:08.000
Amen.

19:08.000 --> 19:10.000
Amen.

19:10.000 --> 19:12.000
All right everybody, now it's your time.

19:12.000 --> 19:19.000
Brothers and sisters, we are gathered here to usher four people into the holy bonds of matrimony.

19:19.000 --> 19:21.000
Get on with it reverend.

19:21.000 --> 19:23.000
These gals ain't getting any younger.

19:23.000 --> 19:29.000
According to the ashes and liabilities, and with the power bested in me by the chairman of the board,

19:29.000 --> 19:39.000
Count Hand, Dusty, Cleo, Elvira, in sickness and in health, and Richard,

19:39.000 --> 19:41.000
I now pronounce you man and wife.

19:41.000 --> 19:43.000
I now pronounce you man and wife.

19:43.000 --> 19:44.000
Glory be.

19:44.000 --> 19:49.000
Hallelujah.

19:49.000 --> 19:51.000
So good.

19:51.000 --> 19:53.000
I just told Mr. Brookhaven it doesn't turn out to be a real reverend.

19:53.000 --> 19:56.000
Wait a minute, we don't want nothing to do with it, but they don't, don't they?

19:56.000 --> 19:57.000
Don't worry about it.

19:57.000 --> 20:07.000
Now listen.

20:07.000 --> 20:09.000
Well, ain't you going to kiss your bride?

20:09.000 --> 20:13.000
Sure, I can't wait.

20:13.000 --> 20:14.000
Hold it.

20:14.000 --> 20:18.000
You are kissing the wrong girl.

20:18.000 --> 20:23.000
I married him to her and her to him.

20:23.000 --> 20:25.000
Well, unmarry him and start over again.

20:25.000 --> 20:27.000
I can't.

20:27.000 --> 20:30.000
I'm authorized to marry people, not to unmarry them.

20:30.000 --> 20:33.000
Well, do you mean to tell me that he is married to my daughter now, Byrie?

20:33.000 --> 20:36.000
I'm afraid so.

20:36.000 --> 20:37.000
Well, you're just a no good skunk.

20:37.000 --> 20:40.000
You planned this to purpose so that you could steal my beautiful bride.

20:40.000 --> 20:43.000
You mean to eat polecat and you picked something you could steal my beautiful Cleo.

20:43.000 --> 20:45.000
You are just a no good barman.

20:45.000 --> 20:46.000
That's what you are.

20:46.000 --> 20:48.000
Well, you're nothing but a no good double O.D.

20:48.000 --> 20:51.000
Why, nobody can talk to me like that.

20:51.000 --> 20:52.000
This calls for a duel.

20:52.000 --> 20:54.000
I just happen to have some pistols in my wagon.

20:54.000 --> 20:55.000
Now, just a minute.

20:55.000 --> 20:57.000
Can't we talk this over?

20:57.000 --> 20:58.000
No chance.

20:58.000 --> 21:03.000
He's demanded satisfaction.

21:03.000 --> 21:06.000
Shall we say 20 paces and fire at will?

21:06.000 --> 21:07.000
Make that 10 paces.

21:07.000 --> 21:10.000
I want to shoot that wife stealing varmint right between the eyes.

21:10.000 --> 21:11.000
Make that five paces.

21:11.000 --> 21:12.000
My honor is at stake.

21:12.000 --> 21:14.000
Five paces it is.

21:14.000 --> 21:20.000
One, two, three, four, five.

21:20.000 --> 21:22.000
They got me.

21:22.000 --> 21:25.000
I'm going to goodbye cruel world.

21:25.000 --> 21:26.000
He got me.

21:26.000 --> 21:28.000
Right in the gizzard.

21:28.000 --> 21:29.000
Gizzard?

21:29.000 --> 21:31.000
Yeah, gizzard.

21:31.000 --> 21:33.000
They're just wounded.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.000
We can nurse them back to hell.

21:35.000 --> 21:36.000
Too late.

21:36.000 --> 21:38.000
They're cold as mackerel.

21:38.000 --> 21:40.000
Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.

21:40.000 --> 21:43.000
Amen.

21:43.000 --> 21:45.000
We sure weren't married long, Cleo.

21:45.000 --> 21:46.000
Well, least ways.

21:46.000 --> 21:50.000
Now we can tell folks we're widows.

21:50.000 --> 21:51.000
Come on, bug.

21:51.000 --> 21:53.000
Let's get the shovels.

21:53.000 --> 21:54.000
No, no.

21:54.000 --> 21:55.000
It's all my fault.

21:55.000 --> 22:17.000
We'll take them to the nearest town and see they get a fitting burial.

22:17.000 --> 22:29.000
Don't mourn brothers and sisters.

22:29.000 --> 22:51.000
Wherever they are, they're thinking of you.

22:51.000 --> 22:52.000
I don't.

22:52.000 --> 22:53.000
I don't.

22:53.000 --> 22:54.000
I don't.

22:54.000 --> 22:55.000
I don't.

22:55.000 --> 22:56.000
That's me.

22:56.000 --> 22:57.000
Shut up.

22:57.000 --> 22:58.000
What?

22:58.000 --> 22:59.000
You get a little sleep, please.

22:59.000 --> 23:00.000
What?

23:00.000 --> 23:03.000
Well, you keep on and I don't, I don't, you know.

23:03.000 --> 23:05.000
Oh, it's having the most terrible dream.

23:05.000 --> 23:08.000
My daughter was being married to Cleo and she kept saying, I do, I do.

23:08.000 --> 23:10.000
And I kept saying, I don't, I don't, I don't.

23:10.000 --> 23:38.000
I don't, I don't, I don't.

